# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3.1 Step 1: Map the problem to quantum circuits and operators "
"{#31-step-1-map-the-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"
msgstr ""
"3.1 Hakbang 1: I-map ang problema sa mga quantum circuit at operator "
"{#31-step-1-map-the-problem-to-quantum-circuits-and-operators}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will use the one defined above from the chemistry context. We start with "
"some general imports.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gagamitin natin ang Hamiltonian na tinukoy natin kanina mula sa konteksto ng"
" chemistry. Magsisimula tayo sa ilang pangkalahatang imports.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Again, we assume the Hamiltonian of interest is known. We will use an "
"extremely small Hamiltonian here, because other methods discussed in this "
"course will be more efficient at solving larger problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Muli, inaasahan nating alam na ang Hamiltonian na gusto natin. Gagamit tayo "
"ng napakaliit na Hamiltonian dito, dahil ang ibang mga pamamaraan na "
"tatalakayin sa kursong ito ay mas mahusay sa paglutas ng mas malalaking "
"problema.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are many prefabricated ansatz choices in Qiskit. We will use "
"```efficient_su2```.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maraming handa nang ansatz na pagpipilian sa Qiskit. Gagamit tayo ng "
"```efficient_su2```.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/vqe/extracted-"
"outputs/84d6380e-8ee8-4340-a416-c07900fe4c5b-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"diagonalization-algorithms/vqe/extracted-"
"outputs/84d6380e-8ee8-4340-a416-c07900fe4c5b-1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Different ansätze will have different entangling structures and different "
"rotation gates. The one shown here uses CNOT gates for entangling, and both "
"Y gates and parametrized RZ gates for rotations. Note the size of this "
"parameter space; it means we must minimize the cost function over 4 "
"variables (the parameters for the RZ gates). This can be scaled up, but not "
"indefinitely. Running a similar problem on 4 qubits, using the default 3 "
"reps for ```efficient_su2``` yields 16 variational parameters.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang iba't ibang ansätze ay may iba't ibang istruktura ng entanglement at "
"iba't ibang rotation gate. Ang ipinapakita rito ay gumagamit ng mga CNOT "
"gate para sa entanglement, at parehong mga Y gate at mga parameterized na RZ"
" gate para sa mga rotasyon. Pansinin ang laki ng parameter space na ito; "
"ibig sabihin nito ay kailangan nating i-minimize ang cost function sa 4 na "
"variable (ang mga parameter para sa mga RZ gate). Maaari itong palakihin, "
"ngunit hindi walang hangganan. Ang pagpapatakbo ng katulad na problema sa 4 "
"na qubit, gamit ang default na 3 reps para sa ```efficient_su2```, ay "
"nagbibigay ng 16 na variational parameter.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"3.2 Step 2: Optimize for target hardware {#32-step-2-optimize-for-target-"
